Text Classification Battle

Project Overview

This project compares four machine learning algorithms for text classification: Decision Tree, K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN), Support Vector Machine (SVM), and Naive Bayes.

The models are implemented using Python in Google Colab and evaluated using the same dataset and TF-IDF feature representation.

Dataset

The project uses the 20 Newsgroups dataset from Scikit-learn.

The following four categories are selected:

* comp.graphics
* rec.sport.baseball
* sci.med
* talk.politics.misc

The dataset contains labelled text documents belonging to these categories.

Algorithms Implemented

1. Decision Tree
2. K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)
3. Support Vector Machine (SVM)
4. Multinomial Naive Bayes

Methodology

1. Load the 20 Newsgroups dataset and select four categories.
2. Preprocess the text using TF-IDF vectorization.
3. Split the dataset into training and testing sets.
4. Train all four classification models using the same dataset and feature representation.
5. Evaluate the models using Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score.
6. Compare the model performances using a table and graph.
7. Analyse the confusion matrix of the best-performing model.
8. Conduct a what-if experiment by changing the SVM regularisation parameter C.
9. Identify the best-performing model based on the recorded experimental results.

Model Comparison Results

The following results were recorded in the experiment.

Algorithm	Accuracy	Precision	Recall	F1-score
Decision Tree	75.34%	75.38%	75.34%	75.26%
KNN	88.15%	88.60%	88.15%	88.13%
SVM	92.01%	92.05%	92.01%	91.98%
Naive Bayes	91.05%	91.07%	91.05%	91.00%

Best-performing model: SVM

Based on the recorded results, SVM achieved the highest accuracy and F1-score among the four classifiers.

What-If Experiment

A what-if experiment was conducted by changing the SVM regularisation parameter C.

The results were compared using the same evaluation metrics to observe the effect of the parameter change on classification performance.

Repository Contents

* text_classification_battle.ipynb — Google Colab notebook containing the implementation and experiments.
* model_comparison.csv — Comparative evaluation results for all four models.
* model_comparison.png — Graph comparing model performance.
* best_model_confusion_matrix.csv — Confusion matrix of the best-performing model.
* svm_what_if_results.csv — Results of the SVM what-if experiment.

Conclusion

This project compares Decision Tree, KNN, SVM, and Naive Bayes for text classification using TF-IDF features.

Based on the recorded experimental results, SVM achieved the best overall performance, with an accuracy of 92.01% and an F1-score of 91.98%.

The project demonstrates the comparison of machine learning classifiers using standard evaluation metrics, confusion matrix analysis, and a what-if experiment.
